    {
      "day": 6,
      "line": "Greta leans in, voice low. \"Here's what we figured out about a raccoon with too many fingers, working at something. Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 6,
      "line": "💡 COUNTER LEARNED — a raccoon with too many fingers, working at something: Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase. (Someone at the haven knew the trick.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 6,
      "line": "📓 Journal: Counter: Buy it off — It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase."
    },
    {
      "day": 10,
      "line": "Word reaches you, days late: Isabella stands accused over what happened to Jose. There's going to be a moot. People are choosing sides."
    },
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "Vera has been talking at the fires. Enough voices — tonight they call a moot. Isabella answers for what happened to Jose."
    },
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "Vera calls the moot. The fire gets built up — word travels fast, and almost everyone comes."
    },
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "The moot turns to you. Your vote matters here — and everyone will remember it."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "The moot doesn't wait forever. Two days of silence from the fire's edge — the count is taken without you."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "The fire is built high. Nobody speaks while the count is taken — you can hear the wind past the edge of the light."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "Vera counts on their fingers, twice, like they don't trust the first number. Then, to the fire: \"0 for guilty. 7 against.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "A long exhale moves around the fire like weather. \"Not guilty — this time.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 17,
      "line": "★ IDENTIFIED: Pokeweed. Smooth stalks, purple-red stems, dark berry clusters. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."
    },
    {
      "day": 40,
      "line": "Isabella spends the afternoon with the vine with elaborate purple-and-white flowers and egg-sized green fruit that wrinkles yellow when ripe — look, smell, the smallest taste, then waiting. Edible, but it argues on the way down. The fire's verdict: food, carefully. Small amounts."
    },
    {
      "day": 78,
      "line": "★ IDENTIFIED: Wild Ramps. Broad smooth leaves, onion smell. Spring only. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."
    },
    {
      "day": 101,
      "line": "📺 SYSTEM: \"\"You CAUGHT the lie AND you can PROVE it?! That's not justice, that's a CHECKMATE! The guilty are lawyering up! PRESENT THE EVIDENCE!\"\""
    }
  ],
